IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sge-p10a-360`

-- Tests of s 360 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: when registration must be refused). Every expected value is written from the text,
-- beside the assertion, before the run. 15 August 2027 plus 30 days is 14 September 2027 (16 days left in August, 14 days into September).

§ `Section 360(1): refusal for want of the requirements`

-- Arguments: satisfied that the minimum requirements have been met; satisfied that all other requirements have been complied with.
-- Satisfied of both: the "if" is not met, so (read as the text's no) no duty to refuse under this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not satisfied of the minimum requirements, or not of the others, or of neither: the Registrar must refuse.
#ASSERT `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The duty to refuse: no time limit and no consequence is stated, so it cannot be breached; a refusal fulfils it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if not satisfied that the requirements have been met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 360(1) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` AT 2

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if not satisfied that the requirements have been met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 360(2) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` AT 2

§ `Section 360(2): refusal on public grounds`

-- (a): either the unlawful purpose or the prejudicial purposes. (b): national security or interest.
#ASSERT `s 360(2)(a) the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for a purpose that the paragraph names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2)(a) the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for a purpose that the paragraph names` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2)(a) the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for a purpose that the paragraph names` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 360(2)(b) the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2)(b) the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The subsection: any one ground makes the refusal a duty; none makes it no duty under this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if satisfied of a ground in the subsection` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 360(2) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` AT 2

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if satisfied of a ground in the subsection` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 360(1) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` AT 2

§ `Section 360(3): appeal to the Minister`

-- Arguments: aggrieved; the decision is the Registrar's under (1) or (2); the date of the decision; the date of the appeal.
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 14 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 20 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 15 9 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not aggrieved, or a decision that is not one under (1) or (2): the right is not given, and the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` FALSE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 20 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE FALSE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 20 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 360(3) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360(3) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 360(3) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` "Lim Wei" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Lim Wei" DOES `s 360(3) appeal to the Minister` AT 30

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 360(3) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` "Lim Wei" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31
